{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1785007854,"nonce":"vCmRYau6vmZX/hoVHQU6DJLoAFA=","title":"oauth: no PKCE on the authorization-code flow","message":"authorize_redirect (crates/scarab-server/src/oauth.rs:46-59) emits response_type/client_id/redirect_uri/state/scope with no `code_challenge`, and the callback (lib.rs:4504) sends no `code_verifier`.\n\nScarab is a confidential client (it holds client_secret), so this is defense-in-depth rather than a break — but PKCE (S256) is the current baseline for authorization-code and some IdPs will start requiring it.\n\nFix: generate a verifier alongside the existing `state`, carry it in the same HttpOnly state cookie (lib.rs:4494), send code_challenge/code_challenge_method=S256 on the redirect, and replay the verifier at the token endpoint.","files":null}]}